\begin{notation}
\label{not:7-46-extra-2}



Products in a Lie group are written multiplicatively, with identity $e$;
additive notation and $0$ are used for abelian examples such as $\mathbb R^n$,
and $I_n$ denotes the identity matrix.
\end{notation}

